Thinking: The user wants a JavaScript function fibonacci(n) for the n-th Fibonacci number, 0-indexed: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, ...


```javascript
function fibonacci(n) {
  if (n < 0) return null;
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  if (n === 1) return 1;
  let a = 0, b = 1;
  for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
    const next = a + b;
    a = b;
    b = next;
  }
  return b;
}
```

